title: 'HRMP: New Deposit Flow'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The relay chain HRMP pallet no longer reserves channel deposits itself. Every call that takes
    or gives back one asks `hrmp::Config::DepositProvider`, a `ChannelDepositProvider` from
    `hrmp-primitives`, for the `DepositTargets` each side should hold, and is finished through
    `OnDepositSet` once they are set. This lets a provider on another chain finish the call later.
    The pallet implements `ChannelDepositProvider` itself for deposits held in `Config::Currency`,
    so `type DepositProvider = Hrmp;` keeps the behaviour of today. Every runtime must now set it.

    With the pallet as its own provider the behaviour is unchanged, except that offboarding a
    recipient now also frees the request slot of a sender that stays, which used to leak.

    Prepares for taking deposits in `pallet-hrmp-para` on the Coretime chain (Asset Hub on Kusama).
crates:
- name: hrmp-primitives
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: major
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-hrmp-relay
  bump: none
